1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:04,300
New Syonan: The Endau Settlement, 1943

2
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:09,412
On the afternoon of the 1st of
February 1944, about 300 people

3
00:00:09,492 --> 00:00:15,525
left occupied Singapore for a stretch
of newly cleared jungle near Endau,

4
00:00:15,605 --> 00:00:19,625
about 150 kilometres up
the east coast of Johor.

5
00:00:19,625 --> 00:00:21,773
The Syonan Shimbun called them

6
00:00:21,853 --> 00:00:24,675
"pioneers in every sense of the word".

7
00:00:24,675 --> 00:00:29,478
They were some 20 families, most of
them from the Bukit Timah district,

8
00:00:29,558 --> 00:00:31,954
46 girls from the Po Leung Kok home,

9
00:00:32,034 --> 00:00:35,668
and a party of labourers and
technicians, sent to grow

10
00:00:35,748 --> 00:00:39,325
food at a settlement that
had been named New Syonan.

11
00:00:39,325 --> 00:00:42,129
Within a year the paper was reporting

12
00:00:42,209 --> 00:00:44,625
more than 7,000 settlers there.

13
00:00:44,625 --> 00:00:47,998
The settlement was an
answer to a simple problem:

14
00:00:48,078 --> 00:00:52,025
Singapore under the Japanese
did not have enough to eat.

15
00:00:52,025 --> 00:00:57,349
Before the war, Singapore and Malaya fed
themselves largely with imported rice,

16
00:00:57,429 --> 00:01:00,575
much of it shipped in
from Burma and Thailand.

17
00:01:00,575 --> 00:01:04,025
The Japanese invasion
destroyed most of the civilian

18
00:01:04,105 --> 00:01:07,283
shipping that had carried
it, and the war at sea

19
00:01:07,363 --> 00:01:10,825
kept supplies short for
the rest of the Occupation.

20
00:01:10,825 --> 00:01:14,909
According to the National
Library's BiblioAsia journal,

21
00:01:14,989 --> 00:01:18,391
the rice ration in Syonan
started at 20 katis,

22
00:01:18,471 --> 00:01:21,575
about 12 kilograms, per person per month.

23
00:01:21,575 --> 00:01:26,337
Towards the end of the Occupation
it had fallen to 8 katis for men,

24
00:01:26,417 --> 00:01:29,806
6 for women and 4 for
each child, and people had

25
00:01:29,886 --> 00:01:34,150
to queue for it in small amounts
whenever supplies arrived.

26
00:01:34,150 --> 00:01:37,737
The administration ran a
"Grow More Food" campaign,

27
00:01:37,817 --> 00:01:42,275
with exhibitions, cheap seeds
and radio talks on how to plant.

28
00:01:42,275 --> 00:01:45,862
Tapioca, sweet potato and
ragi, a kind of millet,

29
00:01:45,942 --> 00:01:49,978
became everyday staples, and
school fields and even the

30
00:01:50,058 --> 00:01:53,950
Padang were turned into
vegetable and tapioca plots.

31
00:01:53,950 --> 00:01:55,800
It was not enough.

32
00:01:55,800 --> 00:02:00,403
In late 1943 the military
administration announced a plan to

33
00:02:00,483 --> 00:02:05,242
move large numbers of people out
of the city to farm the land,

34
00:02:05,322 --> 00:02:09,222
with a goal, according to
the historian Clay Eaton,

35
00:02:09,302 --> 00:02:14,375
of sending as many as 300,000
people from Syonan to rural Malaya.

36
00:02:14,375 --> 00:02:19,067
The task of carrying out the
scheme went to Mamoru Shinozaki,

37
00:02:19,147 --> 00:02:22,587
the Japanese welfare
official who had earlier

38
00:02:22,667 --> 00:02:26,421
brought together the
Oversea Chinese Association,

39
00:02:26,501 --> 00:02:30,725
as told in the post on the
$50 million "gift" of 1942.

40
00:02:30,725 --> 00:02:33,100
Two sites were chosen.

41
00:02:33,100 --> 00:02:37,163
The association was given
responsibility for a settlement for

42
00:02:37,243 --> 00:02:40,491
Chinese families at Endau,
on the coast of Johor,

43
00:02:40,571 --> 00:02:45,245
while a second settlement at Bahau,
in Negri Sembilan, was planned for

44
00:02:45,325 --> 00:02:49,184
Eurasians and Chinese Catholics
under the Eurasian Welfare

45
00:02:49,264 --> 00:02:53,475
Association and the Catholic
Bishop of Malacca, Adrien Devals.

46
00:02:53,475 --> 00:02:57,255
The association put up $2
million to build the farms,

47
00:02:57,335 --> 00:03:02,725
and a construction committee was formed
under its chairman, Lim Boon Keng.

48
00:03:02,725 --> 00:03:07,993
Inspection parties travelled up to
survey the site through late 1943,

49
00:03:08,073 --> 00:03:12,567
and a flag was raised over it
on the 14th of December 1943,

50
00:03:12,647 --> 00:03:16,600
the date later marked as
the settlement's founding.

51
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:20,785
To persuade families to go,
Shinozaki is said to have promised

52
00:03:20,865 --> 00:03:24,705
that the Japanese army would
not interfere, and that rice

53
00:03:24,785 --> 00:03:28,775
would be supplied until the
farms could feed the settlers.

54
00:03:28,775 --> 00:03:32,750
The settlement was run by
the Chinese themselves.

55
00:03:32,750 --> 00:03:37,986
According to a 2020 study of the
settlers' oral histories by Huang Qiuhong,

56
00:03:38,066 --> 00:03:42,805
there were no restrictions on
people's movement in and out of Endau,

57
00:03:42,885 --> 00:03:46,925
unlike at Bahau, where settlers
needed a permit to leave.

58
00:03:46,925 --> 00:03:50,692
The first party left from the
municipal building in Syonan,

59
00:03:50,772 --> 00:03:52,975
where the deputy mayor told them to

60
00:03:53,055 --> 00:03:56,250
set an example for the
settlers who would follow.

61
00:03:56,250 --> 00:04:00,668
Lorry loads of rice, foodstuffs
and farming tools went with them,

62
00:04:00,748 --> 00:04:04,900
and a second group was due to
leave about a fortnight later.

63
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:08,375
Many of the settlers who
followed were city people

64
00:04:08,455 --> 00:04:11,725
with little experience
of farming or building.

65
00:04:11,725 --> 00:04:14,803
On arrival, families lived in longhouses

66
00:04:14,883 --> 00:04:17,725
shared by five to ten families each.

67
00:04:17,725 --> 00:04:20,740
Each family was then
given about three acres,

68
00:04:20,820 --> 00:04:25,143
half of it dry land and half wet
land for rice, and could choose

69
00:04:25,223 --> 00:04:28,800
to stay in the longhouse
or build a home of its own.

70
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:32,378
Settlers grew rice,
tapioca, sweet potatoes and

71
00:04:32,458 --> 00:04:36,350
vegetables such as kangkong,
spinach and tomatoes.

72
00:04:36,350 --> 00:04:39,836
The settlement hospital
handed out medicines free,

73
00:04:39,916 --> 00:04:42,546
and its staff later recalled that what

74
00:04:42,626 --> 00:04:46,050
everyone asked for was
quinine, against malaria.

75
00:04:46,050 --> 00:04:49,058
At first, the association gave each

76
00:04:49,138 --> 00:04:52,050
settler 18 katis of rice a month.

77
00:04:52,050 --> 00:04:55,976
Later, according to the settler
Wan Leong Gay's interview

78
00:04:56,056 --> 00:05:00,123
with the National Archives of
Singapore, it could no longer

79
00:05:00,203 --> 00:05:04,350
supply that much, and the ration
fell to only 4 or 5 katis.

80
00:05:04,350 --> 00:05:08,518
Settlers traded with nearby
Malay villages, and barbers,

81
00:05:08,598 --> 00:05:13,150
pawnshops and small medicine
shops opened in people's homes.

82
00:05:13,150 --> 00:05:18,222
On the 14th of December 1944, the
settlement's first anniversary,

83
00:05:18,302 --> 00:05:23,850
the Syonan Shimbun published an
annual report from its administrators.

84
00:05:23,850 --> 00:05:27,898
It described a "virgin
jungle of a year ago" turned

85
00:05:27,978 --> 00:05:32,025
into a farming colony of
more than 7,000 settlers.

86
00:05:32,025 --> 00:05:36,509
It listed 245 buildings, 50
of them settlers' quarters,

87
00:05:36,589 --> 00:05:41,406
along with a school, a hospital
and a bank, and 5,000 acres

88
00:05:41,486 --> 00:05:46,050
of cleared land, of which
2,000 acres were rice fields.

89
00:05:46,050 --> 00:05:50,175
The report also said that
rice was "in abundance".

90
00:05:50,175 --> 00:05:53,443
That claim sits uneasily
beside the settlers' own

91
00:05:53,523 --> 00:05:57,337
later accounts of the shrinking
ration, and the newspaper

92
00:05:57,417 --> 00:06:00,549
was an instrument of the
occupation government,

93
00:06:00,629 --> 00:06:04,250
so its figures are best read
as the official picture.

94
00:06:04,250 --> 00:06:09,750
Later accounts put the settlement's
population as high as 12,000.

95
00:06:09,750 --> 00:06:12,724
The Malayan People's Anti-Japanese Army,

96
00:06:12,804 --> 00:06:16,924
the guerrilla force led by
the Malayan Communist Party,

97
00:06:17,004 --> 00:06:20,975
regarded the association's
leaders as collaborators.

98
00:06:20,975 --> 00:06:25,400
Convoys travelling between
Syonan and Endau were ambushed.

99
00:06:25,400 --> 00:06:29,966
On the 19th of April 1944,
guerrillas attacked an association

100
00:06:30,046 --> 00:06:34,992
party visiting the settlement and
killed several of its officials,

101
00:06:35,072 --> 00:06:38,953
among them Tan Ean Teck, a
42-year-old rubber trader

102
00:06:39,033 --> 00:06:43,450
who had given to China's war
relief before the Occupation.

103
00:06:43,450 --> 00:06:46,975
He was buried at Bukit
Brown four days later.

104
00:06:46,975 --> 00:06:49,899
Settlers also later recalled officials

105
00:06:49,979 --> 00:06:53,300
being killed inside the settlement itself.

106
00:06:53,300 --> 00:06:58,634
In the end, according to Eaton, it was
Shinozaki, rather than the association,

107
00:06:58,714 --> 00:07:01,619
who negotiated a truce
with the guerrillas,

108
00:07:01,699 --> 00:07:06,975
reportedly by offering them rice in
return for leaving the settlement alone.

109
00:07:06,975 --> 00:07:11,590
The Bahau settlement, which
the Japanese called Fuji-go,

110
00:07:11,670 --> 00:07:15,028
began a month earlier, when its first 150

111
00:07:15,108 --> 00:07:19,300
pioneers left Syonan on
the 28th of December 1943.

112
00:07:19,300 --> 00:07:21,500
It fared much worse.

113
00:07:21,500 --> 00:07:25,505
Its clay soil was hard to farm,
malaria spread through the

114
00:07:25,585 --> 00:07:29,600
settlement within months, and
malnutrition made it worse.

115
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:32,789
Bishop Devals died in January 1945,

116
00:07:32,869 --> 00:07:37,740
and by the end of the war
an estimated 500 of Bahau's

117
00:07:37,820 --> 00:07:41,650
roughly 2,000 to 3,000 settlers had died.

118
00:07:41,650 --> 00:07:46,004
Endau, on the coast, had less
malaria and more fertile ground,

119
00:07:46,084 --> 00:07:50,375
and the association had not
rushed its settlers out as fast.

120
00:07:50,375 --> 00:07:54,050
Bahau's story deserves a post of its own.

121
00:07:54,050 --> 00:07:58,464
When Japan surrendered in
August 1945, the settlers of New

122
00:07:58,544 --> 00:08:03,425
Syonan returned to Singapore,
and the settlement was abandoned.

123
00:08:03,425 --> 00:08:06,925
Singapore still imports
most of what it eats.

124
00:08:06,925 --> 00:08:11,848
According to the Singapore Food
Agency, more than 90 per cent

125
00:08:11,928 --> 00:08:16,442
of its food came from abroad
in 2025, from more than 180

126
00:08:16,522 --> 00:08:21,525
countries and regions, up from
about 140 two decades earlier.

127
00:08:21,525 --> 00:08:25,261
In March 2019, the
government set the "30 by

128
00:08:25,341 --> 00:08:28,729
30" goal of producing 30 per cent of the

129
00:08:28,809 --> 00:08:32,625
country's nutritional
needs locally by 2030.

130
00:08:32,625 --> 00:08:36,899
In November 2025, that goal
was replaced by a new plan,

131
00:08:36,979 --> 00:08:41,174
the Singapore Food Story 2,
with the government citing

132
00:08:41,254 --> 00:08:45,450
high operating costs, limited
land and farm closures.

133
00:08:45,450 --> 00:08:50,328
The new plan aims for local farms
to be able to supply 20 per cent

134
00:08:50,408 --> 00:08:55,437
of the fibre (vegetables, beansprouts
and mushrooms) and 30 per cent

135
00:08:55,517 --> 00:09:00,475
of the protein (eggs and seafood)
that Singapore consumes by 2035.

136
00:09:00,475 --> 00:09:04,027
It sets local farming
alongside three other measures:

137
00:09:04,107 --> 00:09:06,700
buying from a wider range of countries,

138
00:09:06,780 --> 00:09:10,275
keeping stockpiles, and
international partnerships.

139
00:09:10,275 --> 00:09:15,500
The difference from 1944 is
in how the problem is handled.

140
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:18,881
The wartime answer, once
the ships stopped coming,

141
00:09:18,961 --> 00:09:22,975
was to move people out of the
city to grow their own food.

142
00:09:22,975 --> 00:09:26,686
Today's plan is designed
so that no single source of

143
00:09:26,766 --> 00:09:30,914
food can fail, by spreading
imports across many countries,

144
00:09:30,994 --> 00:09:34,275
holding reserves and
growing a share at home.

145
00:09:34,275 --> 00:09:38,148
Why it matters today: New Syonan
is little remembered beside

146
00:09:38,228 --> 00:09:42,100
the darker stories of the
Occupation, yet it shows how close

147
00:09:42,180 --> 00:09:46,646
Singapore came to running out of
food when its supply lines were cut,

148
00:09:46,726 --> 00:09:49,808
and why food security
remains a standing concern

149
00:09:49,888 --> 00:09:53,775
for an island that grows only
a small part of what it eats.
